{"kind":"report","text":"Verdict on the S4 Native evidence plan: NOT SUFFICIENT\n\nI assessed `/private/tmp/artroom-s4-native-remainder-analysis-20261031-v1/PLAN.md`, SHA-256 fef1947e, for request e403bb40. The 149 module records plus a new run of the 104 remaining files can't satisfy the isolated-file follow-up. My note 64d4cb5e gives the same answer, and this verdict replaces it for the record.\n\nWhy it falls short: `docs/testing.md` requires \"the steps the gate never reached\", and gate two never reached Native. The plan itself says that the composed evidence \"cannot become one successful full Native phase\". Its reading of what a module result proves is correct, and that reading is the reason for this verdict. The old 149 files would have no run end, no final rows and no final unhandled-error count.\n\nThe missing proof is one terminal record that covers all 253 files. The bounded witness is one run of compatibility preparation and the unchanged Native stage at a8c409df, tree cea78b8e:\n\n1. Keep the same configs, project order, worker limits, assertions and deadlines.\n2. Use the plan's 128 MiB limit per stream and its 2,400-second budget, and do not mute output.\n3. Retain the interrupted attempt as inconclusive, and report it beside the new run. An overflow stays inconclusive and goes to the planner.\n4. Do not rerun the compilers, the wire owner, Node, Counting or Plain.\n\nThis verdict assesses the evidence plan only. It releases no command, and the builder's own release rules still apply to this run. It does not approve the repair, the final S4 head or either gate, and both ordinary gates stay failed.\n\nParts of the plan that carry over: the 253-file inventory as a selection check, the capture limits and the retention of the attempt. I reviewed the plan's text and did not recheck `files.json` or the selection against the source. A completed run makes the partition unnecessary.\n\n## Architecture\n\nNo design question arises. The plan changes no source. Not applicable.\n\n## Security\n\nThe plan keeps the guards and deadlines and does not mute output. The gap is missing proof of final unhandled errors in the 149 files, which the witness closes. Not sufficient until that run exists.\n\n## Simplification\n\nOne whole run is simpler than a partition, a filter review and a composed report. The witness replaces the plan's proposed follow-up."}